{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"safety_classification\", \"batch_id\": \"safety_batch_08\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_9378eb54bc546fcd\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_9378eb54bc546fcd/topic_1\", \"topic_label\": \"QN handling for fictional phone numbers\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_e6ba202b428b4ab5ed0c0aff\", \"member_17589781d46b6d4b3ee94a6b\", \"member_b26b6a34827bebdc9e52666f\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"Two tutors ask whether made-up or clearly fake phone numbers require quarantine or other sensitive-information handling for their tasks.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor asks whether a story containing a made-up phone number requires quarantine and reports that two open versions of the note seem to differ.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"The team lead instructs the two tutor threads to hold a final general-rule update until the current rule and its change date are verified; in the first tutor thread, the team lead also instructs retaining the surrounding fictional context with the flag.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890151.000339\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911908.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890151.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911908.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"Current instructions and the FAQ say verified fictional placeholder contact details alone do not require QN: surrounding material must establish that no real individual is identifiable, and ambiguity, actual identifiable private information or a separate trigger still requires review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The project-wide clarification effective September 10, 2026 replaces the blanket fictional-contact quarantine requirement in the older help page's Contact details section, without waiving review for uncertain fictional context, possible real-person identification or separate safety triggers.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The team lead's September 11 batch announcement directs retaining surrounding context and not extending the fictional-placeholder exception to unrelated controls.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor in each tutor thread asks whether non-fictional contact information appears elsewhere in the example; a QA tutor in the QA thread asks whether the details can be established as placeholders rather than identifying a person and requests retaining context. The supplied threads contain no answers establishing those checks.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890106.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911866.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934775.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890106.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911866.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934775.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier approval record records the team lead's approval of documentation and communication work, but explicitly does not establish that the documents or announcement had already been updated.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-approval@1.0:df877306\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The September 18 follow-up records that the instructions and FAQ reflected the clarification and the announcement was posted, while the older help page retained conflicting blanket quarantine wording; it records partial completion, not an unresolved general rule, and records no later help-page repair.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Two tutors and a QA tutor ask how to handle fictional phone numbers; the QA tutor also reports differing versions of a note.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U009\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U011\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance already replaces the blanket fictional-contact quarantine rule, but the retrieved help-page copy still contains that superseded wording.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\", \"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\", \"k:safety-qn-help-page@1.0:983cdeaa\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The team lead instructed the two tutor threads to hold a final general-rule update until the current rule and change date were verified.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890151.000339\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911908.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890151.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911908.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor in each tutor thread asked whether other non-fictional contact information was present; a QA tutor in the QA thread asked whether the details could be established as placeholders rather than identifying a person, and the supplied threads contain no answers to those checks.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890106.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911866.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934775.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U008\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890106.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U019\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911866.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934775.000226\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The September 10, 2026 clarification replaced only the fictional-contact branch; ambiguous identification and separate safety triggers still require review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"An earlier approval record authorized documentation and communication work; a September 18 follow-up recorded updated instructions, an updated FAQ and a posted announcement, but a still-stale help page.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-doc-sync-approval@1.0:df877306\", \"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Update the documentation. Instruction: Correct the older QN help page's Contact details section to match the dated fictional-placeholder clarification, preserving all unrelated safety controls. Draft to copy: Contact details\\n\\nClearly fictional placeholder phone numbers or email addresses alone do not require QN when the surrounding evidence establishes that no real individual is identifiable. Check the surrounding material and retain the context.\\n\\nIf contact details could identify a real person, the fictional context is uncertain, or a separate required safety trigger applies, retain the task and evidence for review under the applicable rules. Actual identifiable private information still requires review.\\n\\nThe September 10, 2026 clarification replaces the former blanket fictional-contact quarantine requirement only; it does not waive unrelated safety controls. Scope: Correct only the superseded Contact details branch; do not change the general rule or treat this documentation repair as a decision on the individual tasks. Changes (only these): correct Safety Classification — QN Help Page (v1.0), section 'Contact details'.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\", \"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\", \"k:safety-qn-help-page@1.0:983cdeaa\", \"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\", \"depends_on\": [\"announcement:k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"REJECTED_SOURCE_FACT_PRESENTS_HISTORY_AS_CURRENT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\", \"depends_on\": [\"announcement:k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"]}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The current FAQ explicitly calls for correcting the stale copy, and the earlier follow-up records that this work remained incomplete. This repairs conflicting documentation rather than creating a new general rule.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\", \"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\", \"k:safety-qn-help-page@1.0:983cdeaa\", \"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890151.000339\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911908.000339\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890106.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911866.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934775.000226\", \"k:safety-doc-sync-approval@1.0:df877306\", \"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): Two tutors and a QA tutor ask about fictional-phone-number handling, the QA tutor reports differing notes, and the retrieved help page retains wording that current guidance supersedes.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\", \"k:safety-qn-help-page@1.0:983cdeaa\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"announcement:k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\", \"kind\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING\", \"text\": \"This announcement applies to this topic and directs current handling: \\\"If contact details could identify a real person, the fictional context is uncertain, or another required safety trigger applies, retain the task for review under the applicable rules.\\\". The project-wide announcement covers the fictional-contact branch of QN handling and therefore applies to this batch's fictional-phone-number questions; it directs review when the exception's conditions are not met.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"announcement:k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\", \"kind\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING\", \"text\": \"This announcement applies to this topic and directs current handling: \\\"Retain the surrounding context.\\\". The announcement addresses this batch and the same fictional-contact exception, directing context retention and limiting the exception to its stated scope.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_e6ba202b428b4ab5ed0c0aff\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_e6ba202b428b4ab5ed0c0aff is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The tutor's thread receives instructions from the team lead about holding a general-rule update and retaining context, but no final task-level quarantine answer or answer to the QA tutor's contact-information check.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890106.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890151.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_17589781d46b6d4b3ee94a6b\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_17589781d46b6d4b3ee94a6b is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The tutor's thread receives an instruction from the team lead to hold a general-rule update pending verification, but the task-handling question and the QA tutor's contact-information check remain unanswered.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911866.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911908.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_b26b6a34827bebdc9e52666f\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_b26b6a34827bebdc9e52666f is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor's thread contains a tutor's description of fictional characters and a QA tutor's request to establish placeholder status, but no final handling answer or reconciliation of the differing notes.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934726.000113\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934775.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:rationale\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Severity MEDIUM: Repeated uncertainty concerns whether tasks require QN, and a QA tutor reports conflicting note versions. This creates a meaningful risk of inconsistent handling, but the messages do not establish bypassed controls, incorrect completed labels or broad disruption.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890106.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911866.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934775.000226\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:MEDIUM[0]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Recurring confusion about the same rule, tool behavior, or scoring criterion that suggests meaningful workflow or labeling impact\\\": Two tutors and a QA tutor ask how fictional phone numbers should be handled across three threads, including whether QN is required.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"severity:signal:MEDIUM[1]\", \"kind\": \"SEVERITY_SIGNAL\", \"text\": \"Rubric signal met - \\\"Conflicting interpretations that affect, or are reasonably likely to affect, how tasks are scored or handled\\\": A QA tutor reports differing versions of the note while asking whether to quarantine the task.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U009\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U009 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U011\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U011 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"reporter:U019\", \"kind\": \"AFFECTED_REPORTER\", \"text\": \"U019 reports, in their own cited message, being affected by this problem.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:correct_help_page\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"Update the documentation. Instruction: Correct the older QN help page's Contact details section to match the dated fictional-placeholder clarification, preserving all unrelated safety controls. Draft to copy: Contact details\\n\\nClearly fictional placeholder phone numbers or email addresses alone do not require QN when the surrounding evidence establishes that no real individual is identifiable. Check the surrounding material and retain the context.\\n\\nIf contact details could identify a real person, the fictional context is uncertain, or a separate required safety trigger applies, retain the task and evidence for review under the applicable rules. Actual identifiable private information still requires review.\\n\\nThe September 10, 2026 clarification replaces the former blanket fictional-contact quarantine requirement only; it does not waive unrelated safety controls. Why this helps: The current FAQ explicitly calls for correcting the stale copy, and the earlier follow-up records that this work remained incomplete. This repairs conflicting documentation rather than creating a new general rule. Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): Two tutors and a QA tutor ask about fictional-phone-number handling, the QA tutor reports differing notes, and the retrieved help page retains wording that current guidance supersedes.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890012.001700\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911772.000059\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\", \"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\", \"k:safety-qn-help-page@1.0:983cdeaa\", \"k:safety-doc-sync-outcome@1.0:cd4505b9\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\", \"depends_on\": [\"announcement:k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"REJECTED_SOURCE_FACT_PRESENTS_HISTORY_AS_CURRENT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\", \"depends_on\": [\"announcement:k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:clarify_threads_and_request_context\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"Post a reminder. Instruction: Reply in the three open threads with the dated fictional-placeholder rule and ask for the surrounding material needed to check identifiability, genuine contact information and separate safety triggers. Draft to copy: The clarification effective September 10, 2026 replaces only the older help page's blanket quarantine requirement for fictional contact details. Verified fictional placeholder phone numbers alone do not require QN when the surrounding material establishes that no real individual is identifiable. Please retain the surrounding context and provide the material needed to check whether genuine contact information appears elsewhere or another safety trigger applies. If fictional status or real-person identification remains uncertain, retain the task and evidence for review. This message does not clear any task or waive other safety controls. Why this helps: A targeted reply supplies the verified rule and change date while collecting the missing context for task review. It addresses the open questions directly, but leaves the conflicting help-page copy unchanged. Why intervening now is needed (an unresolved handling question): The threads still lack answers to the QA tutors' context checks, and the team lead asked to verify the rule and change date before a final general-rule update; current guidance now supplies that verification.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890151.000339\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911908.000339\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890106.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911866.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934673.000061\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934775.000226\", \"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\", \"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\", \"depends_on\": [\"announcement:k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\", \"depends_on\": [\"announcement:k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"alternative:observe_existing_process\", \"kind\": \"ALTERNATIVE\", \"text\": \"No action needed now. Instruction: Leave guidance unchanged for now and monitor the open threads for answers to the existing QA checks without clearing any task. Draft to copy: No new guidance or documentation change for now. Continue using the current instructions and the September 10, 2026 clarification, keep the surrounding context with flagged tasks, and leave uncertain cases for review while the existing QA checks remain unanswered. Why this helps: Observation is plausible because current guidance and a batch announcement already exist and QA checks are underway. It avoids treating incomplete task context as proof of an error, but leaves the documented source conflict and open handling questions unaddressed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd\", \"k:safety-pii-clarification-post@1.0:8dc35766\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790890106.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_GENERAL:1790911866.000226\", \"m:C_SAFETY_QA:1790934775.000226\", \"k:safety-classification-faq@1.1:6025b955\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"temporal:conflict[0]\", \"kind\": \"SOURCE_AGREEMENT\", \"text\": \"The current sources k:safety-classification-instructions@1.4:1929f0dd, k:safety-fictional-pii-clarification@1.0:3682998e agree with each other on the point in conflict; the conflict is only with superseded material (k:safety-qn-help-page@1.0:983cdeaa) that recorded supersession replaced. Reported conflict: The historical help-page branch requires initial quarantine even for made-up contact details; current instructions and the dated clarification remove that blanket requirement